  "subtitle": "A free-space 6-DOF mouse you lift into the air and fly — ultrasonic time-of-flight tracks your hand in 3D",
  "why_scout_cares": "The museum's only free-space isotonic 6-DOF pointer: unlike the 2D mice and the isometric force-sensing balls (DLR SpaceMouse) already in the collection, you grip the Logitech 3D Mouse and literally move it through the air — ultrasonic time-of-flight gives X/Y/Z plus pitch/yaw/roll from hand motion alone. A genuine first-of-kind that makes 3D navigation embodied and wand-like.",
